#: includes/settings-page.php:183
msgid "Apply Protection to Post Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:193
msgid "Choose which post types to apply content protection to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:198
msgid "Protection Scope"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:203
msgid "All posts of the selected post types (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:207
msgid "Only posts where protection is turned on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:211
msgid "With \"Only posts where protection is turned on\", nothing is protected until you tick \"Protect this post\" in the Content Protection box of the post editor, or use the \"Turn content protection on\" bulk action on the post list. Only the post types selected above get that box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:213
msgid "In this mode JavaScript Content Protection, Advanced DevTools Blocking and Anti-Screenshot Protection also only load on protected posts, instead of on every page of the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:219
msgid "Content Protection Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:224
msgid "No Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:228
msgid "Encrypt Content (decode via JS)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:232
msgid "Lazy Load (hidden until the browser is verified)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:232
msgid "Encrypting the content helps prevent crawlers from reading raw HTML. Do not enable if you need SEO access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:236
msgid "Lazy Load is the lighter option: the page is sent without the article, and a script fetches it through the REST API once the visitor's browser has been verified. Nothing is encrypted, no decryption key is involved, and if the check fails the visitor gets a Retry button. It stops plain wget/curl scrapers and HTML-only crawlers, and the page stays cache friendly. Scripts inside the article are not executed, as in Encrypt mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:234
msgid "Decryption uses the browser's built-in Web Crypto API. The bundled CryptoJS fallback (about 60 KB) is only loaded on sites not served over HTTPS, or on demand in the rare browser without Web Crypto support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:240
msgid "Loading Skeleton Color Scheme"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:243
msgid "Light (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:244
msgid "Dark"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:245
msgid "Automatic (follow the visitor's system setting)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:248
msgid "Colors of the loading skeleton and the \"enable JavaScript\" notice shown in Encrypt mode until the content is decrypted. Choose Dark for a dark theme. Automatic only fits themes that themselves follow the visitor's system light/dark setting."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: CSS custom property wrapped in <code>, 2: PHP filter name wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:253
msgid "Themes with their own dark mode switch can set CSS custom properties such as %1$s on .icp-protected, or use the %2$s filter. See the plugin FAQ."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:263
msgid "Custom Encryption Key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:266
msgid "Use a unique key for this website. Leave blank to use default key from plugin constant."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:271
msgid "Decryption Key Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:276
msgid "Inline (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:280
msgid "Enhanced (fetch key via REST API after page load)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:284
msgid "Inline puts the key directly in page HTML (simple, works everywhere, but readable via view-source). Enhanced fetches the key from a REST API endpoint instead, keeping it out of cached/static HTML — better against basic scrapers and compatible with full-page caching. Neither mode makes content truly secret to a determined visitor running the page's own JavaScript. This endpoint is not rate-limited by the plugin; use your server/CDN/WAF if you need that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:291
msgid "Enable Headless Browser Detection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:296
msgid "Withhold the content from sessions that look like an automated browser (Puppeteer, Playwright, Selenium)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:299
msgid "Only takes effect when Content Protection Mode is set to Encrypt or Lazy Load — it has no effect in \"No Protection\" mode, since there is no decryption or loading step left to withhold. Scores several client-side automation signals together, so no single false-positive flag can block a real visitor on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:301
msgid "This raises the cost of automated scraping but cannot detect every setup — well-configured \"stealth\" automation tooling can evade individual signals. Treat it as an extra deterrent layer, not a guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:308
msgid "Allow Verified Search Engine Crawlers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:313
msgid "Let Googlebot, Bingbot and other verified search engine crawlers through Headless Browser Detection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:316
msgid "Googlebot renders pages with a headless browser, so without this option it is treated as automation and only sees the loading skeleton instead of your content. A crawler is let through only after your server confirms it with a reverse and forward DNS lookup (the method Google and Bing document). The User-Agent alone is never trusted, so scrapers that pretend to be Googlebot are still blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:318
msgid "Only used when Headless Browser Detection is enabled. Behind a CDN or reverse proxy, check the Visitor IP Detection setting below. The REST API must also stay reachable for crawlers. See the plugin FAQ."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:324
msgid "Visitor IP Detection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:332
msgid "How the plugin finds the real IP address of a visitor, used to verify search engine crawlers. Automatic reads CF-Connecting-IP only when the connection really comes from Cloudflare's published IP ranges, and X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP only when it comes from a proxy or load balancer on a private network, so a visitor cannot forge it. Choose a specific option if your CDN or proxy is not covered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:334
msgid "The proxy header options trust that header completely: only use one when your server accepts traffic from that proxy alone."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: IP address wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:340
msgid "IP address the plugin sees for you: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:341
msgid "unknown"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: IP address wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:349
msgid "Direct connection to your server (REMOTE_ADDR): %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:355
msgid "The first address should be your own public IP. If it is a Cloudflare or proxy address instead, pick the matching option above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:361
msgid "Content Selector (for JS injection)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:364
msgid "Auto-detect"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: example CSS selector wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:369
msgid "CSS selector to locate content wrapper. Used for decryption and JS protection. Example: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:374
msgid "\"Auto-detect\" loads your most recent published post in the background and tests common theme selectors against it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:381
msgid "Enable JavaScript Content Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:386
msgid "Block printing, prevent right-click and text selection, and interfere with browser developer tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:389
msgid "Blocks copying, selecting, printing, and inspecting content via JS. Includes right-click disable, keyboard shortcut blocking (Ctrl/⌘ + C, P, U, etc.), and DevTools interference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:394
msgid "Advanced Browser Protection (Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:398
msgid "Enable Advanced DevTools Blocking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:403
msgid "Actively detect when browser DevTools are opened (not just keyboard shortcuts) and close or redirect away from the tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:406
msgid "Uses the third-party \"disable-devtool\" library alongside the basic protection above. Independent of \"Enable JavaScript Content Protection\" — use either one alone, or both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:408
msgid "When DevTools stay open, this tries to close the tab; if the browser blocks that (the common case, since most browsers only allow closing tabs a script itself opened), it redirects the visitor back to your homepage instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:410
msgid "On the homepage itself the page content is hidden instead of redirected, so a false detection can never cause an endless reload loop."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:417
msgid "Enable Anti-Screenshot Protection (Init AntiSnap)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:422
msgid "Detect scroll-jump and DevTools-triggered layout patterns typical of automated screenshot or scraping tools, and briefly blur the page with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:425
msgid "Real readers scrolling and resizing normally are not affected. The blur clears itself automatically after a few seconds, or as soon as the tab regains focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:427
msgid "Init AntiSnap 6.0 only reacts to the evenly spaced, step-by-step jumps that scroll-and-stitch capture tools make — not to find-in-page, anchor links, scrollbar dragging, zooming, or pop-ups that lock page scrolling."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:434
msgid "Inject Noise"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:439
msgid "Insert invisible junk spans randomly to confuse crawlers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:442
msgid "Invisible to real readers. Class names are generated for each post and change every day, and the rules that hide them are printed in the page itself, so scrapers cannot strip the noise with a fixed list. Some real words are also wrapped in look-alike elements, so removing every unknown element removes real text too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:449
msgid "Noise Injection Rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:453
msgid "Chance (per word) of inserting a noise span. Higher values confuse crawlers more but add more hidden markup to the page. 1–50%, default 7%."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:458
msgid "Sensitive Keywords to Obscure"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: example comma-separated keyword list wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:465
msgid "Enter keywords to hide. Separate by commas. Example: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:470
msgid "These will be replaced visually using CSS pseudo-elements and hidden from raw HTML."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:475
msgid "Global Exceptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:478
msgid "Exclude User Roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:489
msgid "This applies to every protection feature on this page at once — Content Protection Mode, JavaScript Content Protection, Advanced DevTools Blocking, Anti-Screenshot Protection, Inject Noise, and Sensitive Keywords. Selected roles are fully excluded from all of them together and will always see the original, unprotected content — you can't exclude a role from just one feature."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:499
msgid "Important Notes When Using This Plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:501
msgid "Use encryption only if you understand its impact on SEO, caching, and content accessibility."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:502
msgid "JavaScript protection relies on client-side execution. It can be bypassed by experienced users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:503
msgid "For best results, combine multiple protection layers (encryption, JS, keyword cloaking)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:504
msgid "This plugin does not prevent content theft 100%. It raises the difficulty level for scraping."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:505
msgid "DevTools blocking, anti-screenshot detection, and headless browser detection are all heuristic and best-effort. They can occasionally trigger on unusual browsers/extensions, and can be bypassed by a determined user or well-configured automation tooling — treat them as an extra deterrent layer, not a guarantee."
msgstr ""

