msgstr ""

#: init-content-protector.php:189
msgid "This content is no longer available. Please reload the page."
msgstr ""

#: init-content-protector.php:190
msgid "Retry"
msgstr ""

#: includes/verify.php:131
msgid "Please try again in a moment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rest-api.php:207
msgid "This content is protected and is not available through the REST API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:244
msgid "Warning:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:245
msgid "With Encrypt Content or Lazy Load on, the content of protected posts is also withheld from the other places that would hand it out: every WordPress REST API endpoint that renders post content (/wp-json/wp/v2/…, including pages, custom post types and revisions) and the RSS/Atom feeds. The content, and any automatic excerpt, is replaced by a short message there. Mobile apps, headless front ends, feed readers and plugins that read the article that way will receive that message instead. Users who can edit the post and the excluded roles still get the real content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/hooks.php:176
msgid "This content is protected and is only available on the website."
msgstr ""
